<title>USA: Multnomah Cty, Ore., schools yield 5 pct in 2005.</title>
<headline>Multnomah Cty, Ore., schools yield 5 pct in 2005.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seattle Northwest Securities Corp said Tuesday it tentatively priced $96.7 million Multnomah County School District IJ, Ore., general obligation bonds at a top yield of five percent in 2005.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing scale follows:  </p>
<p>    6/1	     Amount	  Coupon	Price</p>
<p>    Maturity	(million)	   (pct)	 (% of par)</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    1999	    $1.000	  4.25	  4.30</p>
<p>						 (approx $ price 99.866)</p>
<p>    2000	    $3.900	  4.25	  4.45</p>
<p>						 (approx $ price 99.311)</p>
<p>    2001	    $5.475	  4.50	  4.60</p>
<p>						 (approx $ price 99.571)</p>
<p>    2002	    $9.150	  4.50	  4.70</p>
<p>						 (approx $ price 98.997)</p>
<p>    2003	    $11.800	 5.00	  4.80</p>
<p>						 (approx $ price 101.132)</p>
<p>    2004	    $30.700	 5.10	  4.90</p>
<p>						 (approx $ price 101.268)</p>
<p>    2005	    $34.675	 5.125	 5.00</p>
<p>						 (approx $ price 100.868)</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
